WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:18.230
Iris Press Publishers, Humpty and His Family by Yulia Puchkova

00:00:18.280 --> 00:00:27.990
Chapter 1 Life in the Egg Hello, I'm an ostrich.

00:00:28.040 --> 00:00:37.870
I'm from Africa, I live in the grasslands, now I'm grown up, but I want to start my

00:00:37.920 --> 00:00:45.270
story from the very beginning, here it is.

00:00:45.320 --> 00:00:52.790
I'm sitting in an egg, it is big and I'm big too.

00:00:52.840 --> 00:00:58.790
I'm tired of sitting here, I want to get out.

00:00:58.840 --> 00:01:05.110
I hit the egg with my beak, but nothing happens.

00:01:05.160 --> 00:01:09.990
It is sometimes light and sometimes dark in the egg.

00:01:10.040 --> 00:01:13.510
When it is dark, I sleep.

00:01:13.560 --> 00:01:19.430
When it is light, I want to go out.

00:01:19.480 --> 00:01:22.430
Now it is very light.

00:01:22.480 --> 00:01:33.790
I hit the egg with my beak again, suddenly there is a small hole in the wall of the egg.

00:01:33.840 --> 00:01:40.150
I take my beak out of the hole and put my eye to it.

00:01:40.200 --> 00:01:43.310
I'm looking through the hole now.

00:01:43.360 --> 00:01:48.870
Wow, it's great there.

00:01:48.920 --> 00:01:59.150
I can see a lot of green grass, some green trees and bushes, there are different animals,

00:01:59.200 --> 00:02:02.510
they are walking in the grass.

00:02:02.560 --> 00:02:10.470
Some animals are eating the grass, some animals are eating the leaves.

00:02:10.520 --> 00:02:16.910
I can see a cheater, it is lying in the tall grass.

00:02:16.960 --> 00:02:31.070
It is hiding from a zebra, the cheater looks very hungry, oh no, it wants to eat the zebra.

00:02:31.120 --> 00:02:42.390
I look at the zebra, it is eating grass, it doesn't see the cheater, I'm very angry.

00:02:42.440 --> 00:02:54.350
I want to get out, I shake the egg, suddenly the egg starts rolling, it is rolling and

00:02:54.400 --> 00:03:00.750
rolling and I'm rolling too, bang.

00:03:00.800 --> 00:03:09.750
The egg hits the cheater on the back, the cheater jumps up, turns around and looks at me.

00:03:09.800 --> 00:03:20.710
Of course, it can't see me, it can see only the egg, it looks and looks and shows me it's

00:03:20.760 --> 00:03:26.950
big, ugly teeth, I'm afraid.

00:03:27.000 --> 00:03:36.630
I'm not looking at it now, I'm hiding inside the egg, I'm very quiet.

00:03:36.680 --> 00:03:46.510
The cheater smells the egg, sneezes and walks away.

00:03:46.560 --> 00:04:01.670
I turn the egg, I can see the zebra now, it is running away, oh no, somebody is rolling

00:04:01.720 --> 00:04:13.630
me back, but I know her, she is my mum, she is big and strong, she is very tall too.

00:04:13.680 --> 00:04:20.750
Now I'm at home again, there are three eggs around me, there is my brother and two sisters

00:04:20.800 --> 00:04:27.910
inside them, it is dark now, I can hear my dad.

00:04:27.960 --> 00:04:37.230
He comes home every evening, he helps my mum a lot, he sits on the nest at night,

00:04:37.280 --> 00:04:53.640
now dad is sitting down on the nest, it is very dark, I'm tired and I sleep.

00:04:54.640 --> 00:05:07.550
There are two others, I wake up and open my eyes, it is light again, I look through the

00:05:07.600 --> 00:05:17.030
hole and see another egg, there is a hole in that egg too, there is an eye in the hole,

00:05:17.080 --> 00:05:27.670
they are looking at each other, now the eye winks at me, I wink too, I shake the egg

00:05:27.720 --> 00:05:35.830
and it starts rolling, my brother does the same, I'm rolling to my brother and he is

00:05:35.880 --> 00:05:45.950
rolling to me, there is a terrible noise, the eggs are a lot of white pieces now and

00:05:46.000 --> 00:05:53.830
we are out, we are free, we are lying on the grass, I put up my beak and say it to my

00:05:53.880 --> 00:06:10.190
brother, hello, hello he answers, our daddy is next to us, hi sons he says, let's give

00:06:10.240 --> 00:06:21.230
you names, he turns away and cries, dear come here, we've got two sons, we must give

00:06:21.280 --> 00:06:31.030
them names, this is the first time I can see our mother in the light, she is big and strong

00:06:31.080 --> 00:06:40.870
like our father, she is beautiful too, she looks at us, winks at our dad and says, let's

00:06:40.920 --> 00:06:53.270
call them Humpty and Dumpty, okay, says dad, but who is Humpty, our mum looks at us again,

00:06:53.320 --> 00:07:04.390
he thinks and says, let's ask them, so which of you is Humpty, me we answer together, no

00:07:04.440 --> 00:07:16.470
says our mum, only one can be Humpty, then I am Dumpty, we say together, my dear says mum,

00:07:16.520 --> 00:07:26.950
we have got a problem with their names, but we have got very good sons, okay, you are Humpty,

00:07:27.000 --> 00:07:38.720
she points at me and you are Dumpty, she points at my brother, now meet each other, says dad, hello,

00:07:39.200 --> 00:07:48.750
I say to my brother, I'm Humpty, nice to meet you, he says, I'm Dumpty, nice to meet you too,

00:07:48.800 --> 00:07:56.270
I say and we shake wings, good chicks say our parents and smile,

00:07:56.320 --> 00:08:16.920
chapter three, naughty legs, Dumpty and I are lying on the grass, dad is looking at us,

00:08:17.720 --> 00:08:34.000
it's time to get up, he says, I get up, now I'm standing, but my legs don't want to stand, they are shaking, I fall down on the grass,

00:08:34.720 --> 00:09:02.590
Dumpty is laughing, it's your turn now says dad, Dumpty stops laughing, now he gets up, but his legs are like mine, they start shaking and he falls down too, he's laughing again, why are you laughing, asks dad, you can't walk?

00:09:02.640 --> 00:09:05.670
It isn't funny.

00:09:05.720 --> 00:09:08.910
But my legs don't listen to me, laughs dumpty.

00:09:08.960 --> 00:09:15.110
Of course they don't, they haven't got any ears, I say, to dumpty.

00:09:15.160 --> 00:09:19.550
Dad looks at me, then, at his legs.

00:09:19.600 --> 00:09:25.430
I haven't got any ears on my legs, but I can walk, he says.

00:09:25.480 --> 00:09:27.330
It is interesting.

00:09:27.380 --> 00:09:29.870
I think, and think.

00:09:29.920 --> 00:09:33.830
Suddenly, I have an idea.

00:09:33.880 --> 00:09:37.550
It is because you listen to your legs, I say.

00:09:37.600 --> 00:09:40.590
You walk when they want to walk.

00:09:40.640 --> 00:09:44.670
Mmm, says Dad.

00:09:44.720 --> 00:09:46.270
What about your legs?

00:09:46.320 --> 00:09:50.190
Don't they want to walk?

00:09:50.240 --> 00:09:53.390
Dumpty and I listen to our legs.

00:09:53.440 --> 00:09:56.510
No, they don't.

00:09:56.560 --> 00:09:58.670
We say together.

00:09:58.720 --> 00:10:02.750
But there are a lot of angry animals around us.

00:10:02.800 --> 00:10:07.670
If you can't run, they can catch and eat you.

00:10:07.720 --> 00:10:09.390
How can they do it?

00:10:09.440 --> 00:10:10.830
Asks dumpty.

00:10:10.880 --> 00:10:14.670
You are always with us.

00:10:14.720 --> 00:10:18.630
Sometimes I sleep, says Dad.

00:10:18.680 --> 00:10:21.430
Then there is mum, I say.

00:10:21.480 --> 00:10:26.470
She sometimes sleeps too, says Dad.

00:10:26.520 --> 00:10:37.830
You can always do it in turn, we say together.

00:10:37.880 --> 00:10:42.910
Chapter four, an ungrateful animal.

00:10:42.960 --> 00:10:45.990
It is a great day today.

00:10:46.040 --> 00:10:49.070
Dumpties and my legs want to walk.

00:10:49.120 --> 00:10:50.870
They like it.

00:10:50.920 --> 00:10:53.310
They start running.

00:10:53.360 --> 00:10:58.030
We always fall down.

00:10:58.080 --> 00:11:01.030
Dad and mum are happy.

00:11:01.080 --> 00:11:05.790
They are looking at us and smiling.

00:11:05.840 --> 00:11:07.990
I start running again.

00:11:08.040 --> 00:11:11.670
Suddenly, I can see a zebra.

00:11:11.720 --> 00:11:14.070
I look and look.

00:11:14.120 --> 00:11:15.270
I know it.

00:11:15.320 --> 00:11:17.030
It is my zebra.

00:11:17.080 --> 00:11:19.870
I run to it.

00:11:19.920 --> 00:11:22.110
Hello, I say.

00:11:22.160 --> 00:11:25.470
I know you, but you don't know me.

00:11:25.520 --> 00:11:28.270
I'm humpty.

00:11:28.320 --> 00:11:34.270
The zebra looks at me and says, but I don't want to know you.

00:11:34.320 --> 00:11:39.070
Why, I ask.

00:11:39.120 --> 00:11:49.350
It is because we, zebras, are beautiful, clever animals, and you, ostriches, are ugly, silly

00:11:49.400 --> 00:11:52.590
words.

00:11:52.640 --> 00:11:54.910
Suddenly I can see dumpties.

00:11:54.960 --> 00:11:56.910
He is next to me now.

00:11:56.960 --> 00:12:00.470
You can hear the zebra's words too.

00:12:00.520 --> 00:12:07.830
First, clever animals don't say bad things about other animals.

00:12:07.880 --> 00:12:10.270
Second, you aren't beautiful.

00:12:10.320 --> 00:12:17.510
You've got a short, thick neck, says he, and no feathers, I say.

00:12:17.560 --> 00:12:21.150
The zebra is angry.

00:12:21.200 --> 00:12:27.350
It wants to hit us, and it runs at us.

00:12:27.400 --> 00:12:29.110
What is it?

00:12:29.160 --> 00:12:31.390
Our legs want to run too.

00:12:31.440 --> 00:12:35.590
Now, we are running very fast.

00:12:35.640 --> 00:12:42.590
Suddenly, our legs turn left, and the zebra turns left too.

00:12:42.640 --> 00:12:45.830
It almost falls.

00:12:45.880 --> 00:12:52.670
When our legs turn right, the zebra can't turn so fast.

00:12:52.720 --> 00:12:54.910
It falls down on the ground.

00:12:54.960 --> 00:12:58.750
Its legs are up in the air.

00:12:58.800 --> 00:13:01.870
We ask, sorry, we can't help you.

00:13:01.920 --> 00:13:03.470
You're too heavy too.

00:13:03.520 --> 00:13:08.310
We cry to it and run away.

00:13:08.360 --> 00:13:10.360
We come to our parents.

00:13:10.440 --> 00:13:17.470
Dad, mum, we can run now, and when we are running very fast, we can certainly turn left

00:13:17.520 --> 00:13:19.990
or right.

00:13:20.040 --> 00:13:23.910
It is very good, say Dad and mum.

00:13:23.960 --> 00:13:25.990
Only ostriches can do that.

00:13:26.040 --> 00:13:28.710
Do you want to know our teacher?

00:13:28.760 --> 00:13:30.390
We ask.

00:13:30.440 --> 00:13:35.150
Yes, they say, who is it?

00:13:35.200 --> 00:13:47.310
It is that funny animal in a striped costume.

00:13:47.360 --> 00:13:50.350
Chapter 5.

00:13:50.400 --> 00:13:54.230
What a name.

00:13:54.280 --> 00:13:57.230
It is very hot today.

00:13:57.280 --> 00:14:02.950
Our parents are standing and we are lying on the grass.

00:14:03.000 --> 00:14:05.350
We are waiting for our sisters.

00:14:05.400 --> 00:14:09.910
They are still inside the eggs.

00:14:09.960 --> 00:14:12.190
Mum and Dad are worried.

00:14:12.240 --> 00:14:17.390
Our sisters must come out, but they don't.

00:14:17.440 --> 00:14:21.150
Can we help them, my brother and I ask?

00:14:21.200 --> 00:14:23.470
We can't help them, say Dad.

00:14:23.520 --> 00:14:25.750
They must do it themselves.

00:14:25.800 --> 00:14:31.950
I'm sure they are girls, say is dumpty.

00:14:32.000 --> 00:14:33.830
How do you know?

00:14:33.880 --> 00:14:34.830
Asks Dad.

00:14:34.880 --> 00:14:38.230
They are not strong.

00:14:38.280 --> 00:14:39.670
Answers my brother.

00:14:39.720 --> 00:14:43.030
Yes, they are weak, I say.

00:14:43.080 --> 00:14:44.830
We must help them.

00:14:44.880 --> 00:14:48.510
I'm sure they can't get out themselves.

00:14:48.560 --> 00:14:52.390
Suddenly, we can hear a noise.

00:14:52.440 --> 00:14:56.310
There are two holes in one of the eggs.

00:14:56.360 --> 00:15:01.390
I can see two beautiful brown eyes in the holes.

00:15:01.440 --> 00:15:03.150
They are looking at me.

00:15:03.200 --> 00:15:05.710
Hello, I say.

00:15:05.760 --> 00:15:07.510
I'm humpty.

00:15:07.560 --> 00:15:09.790
And who are you?

00:15:09.840 --> 00:15:13.310
Mmm, says the egg.

00:15:13.360 --> 00:15:16.110
Then there is a loud noise again.

00:15:16.160 --> 00:15:18.230
And there is no egg now.

00:15:18.280 --> 00:15:22.630
There is a beautiful chick in front of us.

00:15:22.680 --> 00:15:25.590
Of course, it is a girl.

00:15:25.640 --> 00:15:27.790
She is our sister.

00:15:27.840 --> 00:15:33.550
She has got very soft, long feathers and a long, sporty neck.

00:15:33.600 --> 00:15:38.630
Let's call her beauty, says Mum.

00:15:38.680 --> 00:15:42.270
No, says my sister.

00:15:42.320 --> 00:15:45.550
I don't like this name.

00:15:45.600 --> 00:15:48.350
What about feathery?

00:15:48.400 --> 00:15:50.110
Asks Dad.

00:15:50.160 --> 00:15:54.110
No, she says again.

00:15:54.160 --> 00:16:02.750
At this moment, we can hear a terrible noise, and our other sister comes out of the egg.

00:16:02.800 --> 00:16:06.110
She is very beautiful too.

00:16:06.160 --> 00:16:07.830
But she is small.

00:16:07.880 --> 00:16:10.070
She is smiling at us.

00:16:10.120 --> 00:16:13.230
A smile is so nice and kind.

00:16:13.280 --> 00:16:16.830
Hello, smiley, I say.

00:16:16.880 --> 00:16:19.710
Nice to meet you.

00:16:19.760 --> 00:16:23.270
And smiley, she cries and smiles again.

00:16:23.320 --> 00:16:24.990
I like it.

00:16:25.040 --> 00:16:27.230
It's a nice name.

00:16:27.280 --> 00:16:31.950
Good girl, says Mum, but we have a problem with your sister.

00:16:32.000 --> 00:16:35.990
We can't find a name for her.

00:16:36.040 --> 00:16:38.270
Let's ask her, says smiley.

00:16:38.320 --> 00:16:41.030
What's your name?

00:16:41.080 --> 00:16:49.030
Our big sister looks around and sees a very beautiful dragonfly.

00:16:49.080 --> 00:16:50.470
What is this?

00:16:50.520 --> 00:16:51.470
She asks.

00:16:51.520 --> 00:16:56.390
It's a dragonfly, says Mum.

00:16:56.440 --> 00:17:01.910
Then my name is dragonfly, says our sister.

00:17:01.960 --> 00:17:07.310
Oh, it's a very long name, says Dad.

00:17:07.360 --> 00:17:10.030
We must make it short.

00:17:10.080 --> 00:17:13.310
We can call you fly.

00:17:13.360 --> 00:17:17.590
Or dragon, says dumpty.

00:17:17.640 --> 00:17:22.910
Once I don't want to have a dragon in the family, cries Dad.

00:17:22.960 --> 00:17:28.910
And I want to be a dragon, says our sister, and stamps.

00:17:28.960 --> 00:17:33.110
Okay, says Mum.

00:17:33.160 --> 00:17:35.350
Be dragon if you like.

00:17:35.400 --> 00:17:46.750
And she winks at Dad.

00:17:46.800 --> 00:17:52.510
After six, strange grown-ups.

00:17:52.560 --> 00:17:57.310
Today we are going out into the world.

00:17:57.360 --> 00:18:01.550
It is the first time Dad and Mum take us with them.

00:18:01.600 --> 00:18:04.790
We walk together.

00:18:04.840 --> 00:18:09.430
Then we see two very big ostriches.

00:18:09.480 --> 00:18:12.070
They are walking too.

00:18:12.120 --> 00:18:14.960
They are coming to us.

00:18:15.040 --> 00:18:19.310
Now we can see three small chicks with them.

00:18:19.360 --> 00:18:22.830
They are all girls.

00:18:22.880 --> 00:18:25.350
Our parents stop.

00:18:25.400 --> 00:18:28.230
They talk to the big ostriches.

00:18:28.280 --> 00:18:32.670
They say, oh, what beautiful daughters you have got.

00:18:32.720 --> 00:18:41.470
Their necks are so long, their feathers are so soft, their beaks are so thick.

00:18:41.520 --> 00:18:48.670
The big ostriches smile and say, and your daughters are so cute.

00:18:48.720 --> 00:18:57.390
They've got long legs and small bodies, their smiles are so nice, and your sons are so strong,

00:18:57.440 --> 00:19:03.990
their eyes are so clever, their heads are so round.

00:19:04.040 --> 00:19:14.390
I look at my brother, at his eyes and head, and I say, that is not true.

00:19:14.440 --> 00:19:18.230
We can't be strong because we're very small.

00:19:18.280 --> 00:19:25.510
We can't be clever because we're very young, and our heads aren't round because they are

00:19:25.560 --> 00:19:26.990
square.

00:19:27.040 --> 00:19:30.510
Why do you say that?

00:19:30.560 --> 00:19:32.270
Dad is looking at me.

00:19:32.320 --> 00:19:37.470
I can feel that, and he is very angry.

00:19:37.520 --> 00:19:38.990
But why?

00:19:39.040 --> 00:19:48.150
I look at him and ask, Dad, why are you angry with me?

00:19:48.200 --> 00:19:52.270
Because you are rude, my son, he answers.

00:19:52.320 --> 00:19:54.870
Why am I rude?

00:19:54.920 --> 00:19:57.990
I don't know, he says.

00:19:58.040 --> 00:20:06.590
I think it is because you are too small, too young, and your head is too square.

00:20:06.640 --> 00:20:10.110
I don't understand my dad.

00:20:10.160 --> 00:20:21.870
Sometimes grown-ups are so strange.

00:20:21.920 --> 00:20:29.950
In Chapter 7, why does she run away?

00:20:30.000 --> 00:20:33.750
I'm hot and very thirsty.

00:20:33.800 --> 00:20:39.910
I come up to Dad and say, Dad, I'm hot and thirsty.

00:20:39.960 --> 00:20:42.480
Can we go and find water?

00:20:43.480 --> 00:20:52.430
Okay, says Dad, hide under my wings, and tell your brother and sisters to hide there, too.

00:20:52.480 --> 00:21:01.430
Hey, dumpty, smiley, dragon, come here, it's cool under Dad's wings, I cry.

00:21:01.480 --> 00:21:06.480
They run to us, and soon we're all together.

00:21:07.480 --> 00:21:12.430
Let's play, hide and seek, says dumpty.

00:21:12.480 --> 00:21:21.430
Let's, we say, humpty, you must look for us, says dragon.

00:21:21.480 --> 00:21:22.430
Why not?

00:21:22.480 --> 00:21:25.430
I close my eyes.

00:21:25.480 --> 00:21:31.430
It is very funny to hide in Dad's feathers or between his legs.

00:21:31.480 --> 00:21:36.430
First I find dumpty, then I find smiley.

00:21:36.480 --> 00:21:41.430
Oh, I can't find dragon, where is she?

00:21:41.480 --> 00:21:45.430
Suddenly, we can hear a small voice.

00:21:45.480 --> 00:21:49.430
Hello, can I play with you?

00:21:49.480 --> 00:21:53.430
We look and see a cute ostrich girl.

00:21:53.480 --> 00:21:57.430
I like her, and I say, of course you can.

00:21:57.480 --> 00:21:59.430
Can you help me?

00:21:59.480 --> 00:22:04.430
Yes, she says, and smiles, what must I do?

00:22:04.480 --> 00:22:08.430
We must find dragon, I answer.

00:22:08.480 --> 00:22:13.430
The girl starts shaking, then she cries.

00:22:13.480 --> 00:22:15.430
Mommy!

00:22:15.480 --> 00:22:19.430
And runs away.

00:22:19.480 --> 00:22:22.430
I look at dumpty and smiley.

00:22:22.480 --> 00:22:26.430
Why doesn't she want to find dragon, I ask?

00:22:26.480 --> 00:22:30.430
We don't know, they answer.

00:22:30.480 --> 00:22:36.430
Now we are looking for dragon together, but we can't find her.

00:22:36.480 --> 00:22:39.430
Suddenly, I can see dragon.

00:22:39.480 --> 00:22:44.430
She is running between mom's legs and laughing at us.

00:22:44.480 --> 00:22:49.430
I'm very clever, she cries.

00:22:49.480 --> 00:22:53.430
Soon, we come to a big river.

00:22:53.480 --> 00:22:58.430
There are a lot of animals next to the river.

00:22:58.480 --> 00:23:01.430
They are drinking water.

00:23:01.480 --> 00:23:06.430
There are antelopes, giraffes and elephants.

00:23:06.480 --> 00:23:09.430
They are big, but kind.

00:23:09.480 --> 00:23:12.430
There are lions too.

00:23:12.480 --> 00:23:16.430
Dad says they are angry.

00:23:16.480 --> 00:23:22.480
I look at dad, he isn't afraid of lions, he is very brave.

00:23:23.480 --> 00:23:27.430
We come up to the river and drink.

00:23:27.480 --> 00:23:31.430
The water is tasty and cool.

00:23:31.480 --> 00:23:36.430
I want to play with the water, I go into the river.

00:23:36.480 --> 00:23:44.430
Humpty, you mustn't wet your body, cries mom, only your legs.

00:23:44.480 --> 00:23:47.430
My legs are in the water now.

00:23:47.480 --> 00:23:51.480
Smiley is looking at me, she is afraid.

00:23:52.480 --> 00:23:55.430
Smiley, come here I cry.

00:23:55.480 --> 00:23:58.430
The water is soft and kind.

00:23:58.480 --> 00:24:01.430
My legs like it.

00:24:01.480 --> 00:24:05.430
Smiley goes into the water, she likes it.

00:24:05.480 --> 00:24:08.430
Dumpety is in the water too.

00:24:08.480 --> 00:24:12.430
Now all our legs are in the water.

00:24:12.480 --> 00:24:17.430
Suddenly, we can hear the small voice again.

00:24:17.480 --> 00:24:20.430
Can I play with you?

00:24:20.480 --> 00:24:25.430
I turn round and see that cute ostrich girl.

00:24:25.480 --> 00:24:28.430
I'm happy to see you again, I say.

00:24:28.480 --> 00:24:30.430
Let's play together.

00:24:30.480 --> 00:24:36.430
I'm Humpty, this is Smiley and that is Dumpty.

00:24:36.480 --> 00:24:38.430
Nice to meet you.

00:24:38.480 --> 00:24:44.480
I'm softy, says the girl and smiles.

00:24:45.480 --> 00:24:50.430
Wait, say Smiley, we can't start playing, we must call Dragon.

00:24:50.480 --> 00:24:52.430
Dragon, we cry.

00:24:52.480 --> 00:24:54.430
Dragon, come here.

00:24:54.480 --> 00:24:58.430
There she is, Dragon is running to us.

00:24:58.480 --> 00:25:01.430
Dragon, I say, we've got a friend.

00:25:01.480 --> 00:25:05.430
Her name is softy.

00:25:05.480 --> 00:25:10.430
I turn my head, but there is no softy.

00:25:10.480 --> 00:25:14.430
Where is your friend, asks Dragon.

00:25:14.480 --> 00:25:19.430
I don't know, I say and look around.

00:25:19.480 --> 00:25:22.430
Suddenly, I can see softy.

00:25:22.480 --> 00:25:27.430
She's running away, very fast.

00:25:27.480 --> 00:25:33.430
I'm very sad, I don't know why, but I like softy.

00:25:33.480 --> 00:25:37.430
I think she's very strange.

00:25:37.480 --> 00:25:44.430
First, she wants to play with us, but then she always runs away.

00:25:44.480 --> 00:25:46.480
Why?

00:25:53.480 --> 00:25:56.430
Chapter 8

00:25:56.480 --> 00:26:00.430
Living Stones

00:26:00.480 --> 00:26:04.430
We're standing with our legs in the river.

00:26:04.480 --> 00:26:08.430
Dragon is looking at the water.

00:26:08.480 --> 00:26:22.430
Suddenly, she says, look, there are big brown stones in the water.

00:26:22.480 --> 00:26:28.430
I look at the stones, they are very interesting.

00:26:28.480 --> 00:26:35.430
Dragon, have stones got eyes, I ask.

00:26:35.480 --> 00:26:39.430
Of course they haven't, she answers.

00:26:39.480 --> 00:26:49.430
Dragon, have stones got ears, I ask my second question.

00:26:49.480 --> 00:26:54.430
Of course they haven't, you are so silly, Humpty.

00:26:54.480 --> 00:27:03.430
Dragon, have stones got nostrils, I ask my third question.

00:27:03.480 --> 00:27:11.430
She looks at me, puts her wing to her head and turns it there three times.

00:27:11.480 --> 00:27:17.430
Then you aren't standing on a stone, I say.

00:27:17.480 --> 00:27:23.430
Because your stone is looking at me and listening to us

00:27:23.480 --> 00:27:28.430
and it has got a big nose.

00:27:28.480 --> 00:27:40.430
Ha ha ha, cries Dragon, you are too hot.

00:27:40.480 --> 00:27:45.430
Turn your head down and look, I say.

00:27:45.480 --> 00:27:50.430
Now, Dragon is looking at the stone under her toes

00:27:50.480 --> 00:27:56.430
and the stone is looking at her, their eyes meet.

00:27:56.480 --> 00:28:01.430
Dragon is afraid, she is shaking.

00:28:01.480 --> 00:28:11.430
Hello, she whispers, hmm, says the stone.

00:28:11.480 --> 00:28:15.480
Mummy!

00:28:16.480 --> 00:28:25.430
Cries Dragon and jumps off the stone.

00:28:25.480 --> 00:28:31.430
The stone starts growing, it grows and grows.

00:28:31.480 --> 00:28:38.430
Now it has got a fat body and a very big mouth.

00:28:38.480 --> 00:28:44.430
Hello, I'm a hippo, says the stone.

00:28:44.480 --> 00:28:48.430
And I'm Dragon, says my sister.

00:28:48.480 --> 00:28:54.430
Dragon asks the hippo and starts shaking.

00:28:54.480 --> 00:29:00.430
Oh, I'm so afraid, please don't eat me, Dragon.

00:29:00.480 --> 00:29:06.430
Now, he is laughing, but he looks very kind.

00:29:06.480 --> 00:29:12.430
I understand, he is playing with Dragon.

00:29:12.480 --> 00:29:18.430
Dragon is very angry, she thinks he is laughing at her.

00:29:18.480 --> 00:29:20.430
Let's go, chicks.

00:29:20.480 --> 00:29:26.430
She says to us, it's silly to talk to a stone.

00:29:26.480 --> 00:29:32.430
The hippo can hear her words, he stops laughing.

00:29:32.480 --> 00:29:38.430
Now, he looks sad, he says,

00:29:38.480 --> 00:29:42.430
that's why we live under water.

00:29:42.480 --> 00:29:48.430
And he goes under the water again.

00:29:48.480 --> 00:29:51.430
I feel very bad.

00:29:51.480 --> 00:30:03.480
My sister is sometimes so rude.

00:30:04.480 --> 00:30:08.430
Chapter 9

00:30:08.480 --> 00:30:13.430
They want to live too.

00:30:13.480 --> 00:30:17.430
I want to see Softie.

00:30:17.480 --> 00:30:21.430
I want to ask her why she always runs away.

00:30:21.480 --> 00:30:24.430
I look around.

00:30:24.480 --> 00:30:32.430
I can't see her in the river, I can't see her near the river.

00:30:32.480 --> 00:30:34.430
I'm very sad.

00:30:34.480 --> 00:30:39.430
Let's go home, says Mum.

00:30:39.480 --> 00:30:45.430
We get out of the water and walk home with Mum and Dad.

00:30:45.480 --> 00:30:51.430
Suddenly, a very small, green animal jumps at me.

00:30:51.480 --> 00:30:54.430
It is very funny.

00:30:54.480 --> 00:31:01.430
It has got four short legs and two very long and strong legs.

00:31:01.480 --> 00:31:05.430
It has got very big, funny eyes too.

00:31:05.480 --> 00:31:09.430
What's this? I ask Dad.

00:31:09.480 --> 00:31:11.430
It's food, he answers.

00:31:11.480 --> 00:31:13.430
Very tasty food.

00:31:13.480 --> 00:31:15.430
Eat it.

00:31:15.480 --> 00:31:18.430
I look at the animal.

00:31:18.480 --> 00:31:24.430
It is sitting on my left leg and making a funny noise.

00:31:24.480 --> 00:31:26.430
I can't eat it.

00:31:26.480 --> 00:31:30.430
I'm sure it wants to live.

00:31:30.480 --> 00:31:33.430
Suddenly, I can see a big beak.

00:31:33.480 --> 00:31:39.430
The beak opens and catches the animal.

00:31:39.480 --> 00:31:42.430
Oh no, I cry.

00:31:42.480 --> 00:31:44.430
I can see Dragon.

00:31:44.480 --> 00:31:48.430
The green animal is inside her beak.

00:31:48.480 --> 00:31:51.430
What are you doing, I cry?

00:31:51.480 --> 00:31:55.430
Open your beak.

00:31:55.480 --> 00:31:58.430
Answers Dragon.

00:31:58.480 --> 00:32:03.430
Then I take Dragon by the legs and shake her.

00:32:03.480 --> 00:32:09.430
Her beak opens and the green animal jumps out.

00:32:09.480 --> 00:32:14.430
Are you crazy, cries Dragon?

00:32:14.480 --> 00:32:18.430
I'm fine and you aren't kind, I say.

00:32:18.480 --> 00:32:24.430
Look, there are a lot of seeds and fruit in the grasslands.

00:32:24.480 --> 00:32:27.430
Why do you want to eat an animal?

00:32:27.480 --> 00:32:31.430
Because I like it, says Dragon.

00:32:31.480 --> 00:32:33.430
No, you don't.

00:32:33.480 --> 00:32:39.430
When you like somebody, you want to play with her or talk to her.

00:32:39.480 --> 00:32:43.430
You don't want to eat her.

00:32:43.480 --> 00:32:47.430
Laughs, Dragon.

00:32:47.480 --> 00:32:50.430
Humpty is in love.

00:32:50.480 --> 00:32:53.430
Dumpty, smiley, listen.

00:32:53.480 --> 00:32:56.430
Humpty is in love.

00:32:56.480 --> 00:32:58.430
Who is she?

00:32:58.480 --> 00:33:00.430
Tell us.

00:33:00.480 --> 00:33:05.430
Now, I am very angry.

00:33:05.480 --> 00:33:09.430
I want to hit Dragon, but I can't.

00:33:09.480 --> 00:33:12.430
She's a girl.

00:33:12.480 --> 00:33:15.430
Smiley looks at me.

00:33:15.480 --> 00:33:21.430
She understands me and she says, I'm in love too.

00:33:21.480 --> 00:33:25.430
It is so nice to be in love.

00:33:25.480 --> 00:33:28.430
My brother, Dumpty, looks at us.

00:33:28.480 --> 00:33:34.430
Then at Dragon and says, I'm in love too.

00:33:34.480 --> 00:33:38.480
That's a pity you are not, Dragon.

00:33:45.480 --> 00:33:47.430
Chapter 10.

00:33:47.480 --> 00:33:51.430
When we are together,

00:33:51.480 --> 00:33:59.430
today, Mum and Dad are at home, and we are not.

00:33:59.480 --> 00:34:02.430
We are walking and looking around.

00:34:02.480 --> 00:34:07.480
It is very interesting in the grasslands.

00:34:09.480 --> 00:34:12.430
I look at the grass.

00:34:12.480 --> 00:34:16.430
There are a lot of those green animals there.

00:34:16.480 --> 00:34:20.430
Mum says they are insects.

00:34:20.480 --> 00:34:25.430
My green animal's name is a grasshopper.

00:34:25.480 --> 00:34:28.430
There are other animals too.

00:34:28.480 --> 00:34:31.430
I can see ants.

00:34:31.480 --> 00:34:36.430
Butterflies, spiders and snails.

00:34:36.480 --> 00:34:38.430
Some grasshoppers are jumping.

00:34:38.480 --> 00:34:41.430
Some are singing.

00:34:41.480 --> 00:34:43.430
The ants are working.

00:34:43.480 --> 00:34:46.430
The butterflies are flying.

00:34:46.480 --> 00:34:48.430
The spiders are hunting.

00:34:48.480 --> 00:34:51.430
The snails are lazy.

00:34:51.480 --> 00:34:56.430
They are sleeping on the leaves or grass.

00:34:56.480 --> 00:35:02.430
Together we are watching insects and other animals.

00:35:02.480 --> 00:35:06.430
Only Dragon is not with us.

00:35:06.480 --> 00:35:09.430
She doesn't like watching small animals.

00:35:09.480 --> 00:35:12.430
She likes eating them.

00:35:12.480 --> 00:35:16.430
She can even eat a lizard.

00:35:16.480 --> 00:35:18.430
We are very quiet.

00:35:18.480 --> 00:35:23.430
A butterfly sits down on Smiley's wing.

00:35:23.480 --> 00:35:27.430
It is so beautiful.

00:35:27.480 --> 00:35:32.430
Suddenly, I can feel danger.

00:35:32.480 --> 00:35:40.430
We are watching a butterfly, and the lioness is watching us.

00:35:40.480 --> 00:35:45.430
Smiley, dumpty, I whisper.

00:35:45.480 --> 00:35:50.430
There is a lioness behind us.

00:35:50.480 --> 00:35:55.430
She is hiding in the bushes.

00:35:55.480 --> 00:35:57.430
They look at me.

00:35:57.480 --> 00:36:01.430
They are afraid.

00:36:01.480 --> 00:36:03.430
What can we do?

00:36:03.480 --> 00:36:06.430
They whisper to me.

00:36:06.480 --> 00:36:12.430
We must run very fast, and we must stay together.

00:36:12.480 --> 00:36:18.430
Now we are running, and the lioness is running after us.

00:36:18.480 --> 00:36:23.430
We can hear her behind us.

00:36:23.480 --> 00:36:27.430
Humpty, she can catch us, cries Smiley.

00:36:27.480 --> 00:36:30.430
Suddenly, I have an idea.

00:36:30.480 --> 00:36:33.430
Stop chicks, I cry.

00:36:33.480 --> 00:36:40.430
We must turn with our backs to each other, and stand in a circle, wing in wing.

00:36:40.480 --> 00:36:47.430
When the lioness jumps at you, you lie on the backs, and kick her with your legs.

00:36:47.480 --> 00:36:50.430
So, we stand in a circle.

00:36:50.480 --> 00:36:54.430
I can feel my brothers and sisters' backs behind.

00:36:54.480 --> 00:36:57.430
The lioness runs at me.

00:36:57.480 --> 00:37:00.430
Then she jumps at me.

00:37:00.480 --> 00:37:05.430
Now my friend backs, and give her a strong kick.

00:37:05.480 --> 00:37:07.430
The lioness flies away.

00:37:07.480 --> 00:37:11.430
Fly, lioness, fly.

00:37:11.480 --> 00:37:16.430
Now she is very angry.

00:37:16.480 --> 00:37:18.430
She is running around us.

00:37:18.480 --> 00:37:22.430
But every time, when she jumps at us,

00:37:22.480 --> 00:37:27.430
she gets a strong kick and flies away.

00:37:27.480 --> 00:37:30.430
The lioness comes back again.

00:37:30.480 --> 00:37:33.430
It is strange.

00:37:33.480 --> 00:37:37.430
I think she likes flying.

00:37:37.480 --> 00:37:40.430
At last, she is very tired.

00:37:40.480 --> 00:37:42.430
She can't catch us.

00:37:42.480 --> 00:37:47.430
She is still angry, but she walks away.

00:37:47.480 --> 00:37:52.430
Well done, Humpty, say my brother and sister.

00:37:52.480 --> 00:37:56.430
Well done, dumped in Smiley, I say.

00:37:56.480 --> 00:37:58.430
We are very proud today.

00:37:58.480 --> 00:38:02.430
We are only small, young ostriches.

00:38:02.480 --> 00:38:07.480
But when we are together, we can fight a lion.

00:38:14.480 --> 00:38:16.430
Chapter 11.

00:38:16.480 --> 00:38:19.430
A race.

00:38:19.480 --> 00:38:24.430
We are at home again.

00:38:24.480 --> 00:38:26.430
But we don't want to have a rest.

00:38:26.480 --> 00:38:29.430
We want to run and play.

00:38:29.480 --> 00:38:37.430
Dad looks at us, smiles and says, let's have a race.

00:38:37.480 --> 00:38:41.430
What is a race, I ask?

00:38:41.480 --> 00:38:46.430
It's when all the chicks run together to their mum.

00:38:46.480 --> 00:38:51.430
And one of them comes the first, says Dad.

00:38:51.480 --> 00:38:55.430
I want to be the first, says Dragon.

00:38:55.480 --> 00:38:59.430
I want to be the first, too, says Dumpty.

00:38:59.480 --> 00:39:02.430
And I can be the fourth, says Smiley.

00:39:02.480 --> 00:39:04.430
I don't want to be the first.

00:39:04.480 --> 00:39:08.430
And you, Humpty, asks Dad.

00:39:08.480 --> 00:39:10.430
I want to run.

00:39:10.480 --> 00:39:13.430
I like running, I answer.

00:39:13.480 --> 00:39:17.430
Then let's start, stand next to each other.

00:39:17.480 --> 00:39:22.430
One, two, three, go.

00:39:22.480 --> 00:39:25.430
We all start running to mum.

00:39:25.480 --> 00:39:29.430
She's standing very far away.

00:39:29.480 --> 00:39:32.430
Smiley is running the first.

00:39:32.480 --> 00:39:34.430
She's in front of me.

00:39:34.480 --> 00:39:37.430
I look behind and see Dumpty.

00:39:37.480 --> 00:39:40.430
He's the third.

00:39:40.480 --> 00:39:44.430
Then there is Dragon.

00:39:44.480 --> 00:39:47.430
Suddenly, Dragon cries.

00:39:47.480 --> 00:39:49.430
Oh, my stomach.

00:39:49.480 --> 00:39:51.430
We turn our heads.

00:39:51.480 --> 00:39:54.430
Dragon falls on the ground and starts rolling.

00:39:54.480 --> 00:39:56.430
Oh, chicks, help me.

00:39:56.480 --> 00:40:00.430
I've got an awful stomachache.

00:40:00.480 --> 00:40:02.430
We run to Dragon.

00:40:02.480 --> 00:40:04.430
She looks terrible.

00:40:04.480 --> 00:40:06.430
All her feathers are dirty.

00:40:06.480 --> 00:40:09.430
Her eyes are closed.

00:40:09.480 --> 00:40:13.430
Suddenly, she opens them.

00:40:13.480 --> 00:40:16.430
Oh, dear brothers and sister.

00:40:16.480 --> 00:40:20.430
Help me to get up, please, she says.

00:40:20.480 --> 00:40:22.430
We look at each other.

00:40:22.480 --> 00:40:27.430
It is the first time Dragon says please.

00:40:27.480 --> 00:40:30.430
And it is very strange.

00:40:30.480 --> 00:40:34.430
We take her by the wings and help her.

00:40:34.480 --> 00:40:36.430
Thank you, she says.

00:40:36.480 --> 00:40:40.430
Now, stand behind me, please.

00:40:40.480 --> 00:40:44.430
I'm afraid I can fall on my back.

00:40:44.480 --> 00:40:46.430
What's the matter with Dragon?

00:40:46.480 --> 00:40:49.430
Now, she says, thank you.

00:40:49.480 --> 00:40:52.430
I'm sure she is really ill.

00:40:52.480 --> 00:40:56.430
We stand behind her.

00:40:56.480 --> 00:41:00.430
Thank you, she says again.

00:41:00.480 --> 00:41:02.430
I think my stomach is okay now.

00:41:02.480 --> 00:41:06.430
One, two, three, go.

00:41:06.480 --> 00:41:09.430
She cries and starts running.

00:41:09.480 --> 00:41:11.430
We look at each other.

00:41:11.480 --> 00:41:15.430
Then we understand everything.

00:41:15.480 --> 00:41:17.430
Naughty Dragon.

00:41:17.480 --> 00:41:19.430
We start running too.

00:41:19.480 --> 00:41:23.430
Dragon turns her head and laughs.

00:41:23.480 --> 00:41:25.430
You're too silly.

00:41:25.480 --> 00:41:28.430
My brothers and sister.

00:41:28.480 --> 00:41:33.430
Suddenly, she's quiet.

00:41:33.480 --> 00:41:38.430
She stops running and sits down on the grass.

00:41:38.480 --> 00:41:42.430
Smiley and I are next to her now.

00:41:42.480 --> 00:41:44.430
We can hear a noise.

00:41:44.480 --> 00:41:46.430
Dragon is coughing.

00:41:46.480 --> 00:41:49.430
Her cough is terrible.

00:41:49.480 --> 00:41:52.430
Now, dumpty is with us too.

00:41:52.480 --> 00:41:58.430
We all hit her on the back, again and again.

00:41:58.480 --> 00:42:05.430
Suddenly, a beautiful, big butterfly flies out of her beak.

00:42:05.480 --> 00:42:09.430
Food is escaping, cries Dragon

00:42:09.480 --> 00:42:14.430
and wants to get up but starts coughing again.

00:42:14.480 --> 00:42:18.430
This time, an orange dragon fly

00:42:18.480 --> 00:42:21.430
and a purple fly come out.

00:42:21.480 --> 00:42:25.430
Then a fat grasshopper jumps out.

00:42:25.480 --> 00:42:29.430
Now, Dragon stops coughing.

00:42:29.480 --> 00:42:33.430
Again, that green animal, she cries

00:42:33.480 --> 00:42:37.430
and runs after the poor grasshopper.

00:42:37.480 --> 00:42:41.430
She keeps her mouth open when she's running, says Smiley.

00:42:41.480 --> 00:42:44.430
It's very dangerous.

00:42:44.480 --> 00:42:46.430
Yes, I say.

00:42:46.480 --> 00:42:49.480
Especially for insects.

00:42:56.480 --> 00:42:58.430
Chapter 12.

00:42:58.480 --> 00:43:01.430
A storm.

00:43:01.480 --> 00:43:03.430
It is afternoon.

00:43:03.480 --> 00:43:06.430
It is very hot.

00:43:06.480 --> 00:43:08.430
We are at home.

00:43:08.480 --> 00:43:11.430
We are hiding under Dad's wings.

00:43:11.480 --> 00:43:14.430
Mum is away.

00:43:14.480 --> 00:43:16.430
What is it?

00:43:16.480 --> 00:43:19.430
The sky isn't blue now.

00:43:19.480 --> 00:43:22.430
It is black.

00:43:22.480 --> 00:43:24.430
What's the matter?

00:43:24.480 --> 00:43:27.430
I ask Dad.

00:43:27.480 --> 00:43:31.430
There are clouds in the sky, says Dad.

00:43:31.480 --> 00:43:33.430
But why is it so dark?

00:43:33.480 --> 00:43:36.430
Ask Stunty.

00:43:36.480 --> 00:43:42.430
It's because the clouds are covering the sun and says Dad.

00:43:42.480 --> 00:43:47.430
Suddenly, we can feel the air.

00:43:47.480 --> 00:43:52.430
The air is running.

00:43:52.480 --> 00:43:56.430
Is the air afraid of the clouds, I ask Dad.

00:43:56.480 --> 00:43:59.430
Why is it running?

00:43:59.480 --> 00:44:02.430
Dad smiles and answers.

00:44:02.480 --> 00:44:06.430
The running air is the wind.

00:44:06.480 --> 00:44:14.430
I don't know why, but it's always very windy before a storm.

00:44:14.480 --> 00:44:16.430
What is a storm?

00:44:16.480 --> 00:44:19.430
Ask Smiley.

00:44:19.480 --> 00:44:21.430
She's shaking.

00:44:21.480 --> 00:44:24.430
She's afraid of the strong wind.

00:44:24.480 --> 00:44:28.430
She doesn't like the black clouds.

00:44:28.480 --> 00:44:34.430
A storm is Dad starts and stops.

00:44:34.480 --> 00:44:38.430
I can feel water on my beak.

00:44:38.480 --> 00:44:46.430
Chicks hide under my body, cries Dad, and stand next to each other.

00:44:46.480 --> 00:44:49.430
Why must I stand next to them?

00:44:49.480 --> 00:44:51.430
Ask Stragon.

00:44:51.480 --> 00:44:54.430
She doesn't want to listen to Dad.

00:44:54.480 --> 00:44:56.430
Dad is angry.

00:44:56.480 --> 00:44:58.430
Do what I say.

00:44:58.480 --> 00:45:00.430
He cries to dragon.

00:45:00.480 --> 00:45:05.430
You mustn't walk in the rain.

00:45:05.480 --> 00:45:11.430
This is only water, she says, and runs from under Dad's wing.

00:45:11.480 --> 00:45:14.430
Look.

00:45:14.480 --> 00:45:16.430
The air isn't hot now.

00:45:16.480 --> 00:45:18.430
It's cool.

00:45:18.480 --> 00:45:21.430
And the water is cool too.

00:45:21.480 --> 00:45:23.430
The rain is funny.

00:45:23.480 --> 00:45:26.430
But I must listen to Dad.

00:45:26.480 --> 00:45:28.430
So I don't go to dragon.

00:45:28.480 --> 00:45:31.430
Don't putty and smiley.

00:45:31.480 --> 00:45:33.430
Listen to Dad too.

00:45:33.480 --> 00:45:36.430
They're under his body.

00:45:36.480 --> 00:45:40.430
You are afraid of the water, cries dragon.

00:45:40.480 --> 00:45:45.430
She is dancing in the rain and laughing at us.

00:45:45.480 --> 00:45:51.430
You remember, when we go to the river, we never wet our bodies.

00:45:51.480 --> 00:45:54.430
Now dragon is all wet.

00:45:54.480 --> 00:45:56.430
Her head is wet.

00:45:56.480 --> 00:45:58.430
Her body is wet.

00:45:58.480 --> 00:46:01.430
And her wings are wet.

00:46:01.480 --> 00:46:06.430
The water is running down her beak and her legs.

00:46:06.480 --> 00:46:09.430
We can't see any feathers.

00:46:09.480 --> 00:46:12.430
Where are they?

00:46:12.480 --> 00:46:16.430
Dragon isn't dragon anymore.

00:46:16.480 --> 00:46:19.430
She's thin and ugly.

00:46:19.480 --> 00:46:23.430
Her head is very small now.

00:46:23.480 --> 00:46:28.430
She's shaking because she's laughing at us.

00:46:28.480 --> 00:46:33.430
When she laughs, we only can see her big open beak.

00:46:33.480 --> 00:46:37.430
It is so big and her neck is so thin.

00:46:37.480 --> 00:46:40.430
We close our eyes and open them again.

00:46:40.480 --> 00:46:42.430
But nothing changes.

00:46:42.480 --> 00:46:44.430
There is no dragon.

00:46:44.480 --> 00:46:48.430
Only that's ugly laughing bird.

00:46:48.480 --> 00:46:53.430
Suddenly the rain stops.

00:46:53.480 --> 00:46:57.430
But the air is still very cool.

00:46:57.480 --> 00:47:00.430
Soon our mum comes.

00:47:00.480 --> 00:47:03.430
She looks at the bird and cries.

00:47:03.480 --> 00:47:05.430
Who is that?

00:47:05.480 --> 00:47:08.430
That's dragon answers dad.

00:47:08.480 --> 00:47:13.430
Our dragon asks mum and her beak opens.

00:47:13.480 --> 00:47:17.430
Of course, ours says dad.

00:47:17.480 --> 00:47:22.480
No other ostriches have got dragons in their families.

00:47:23.480 --> 00:47:32.430
Chapter 13.

00:47:32.480 --> 00:47:35.430
Magic.

00:47:35.480 --> 00:47:39.430
We wake up and open our eyes.

00:47:39.480 --> 00:47:41.430
It is morning.

00:47:41.480 --> 00:47:45.430
It is sunny and warm again.

00:47:45.480 --> 00:47:49.430
Let's play tag, says smiley.

00:47:49.480 --> 00:47:53.430
She likes playing tag because she runs very fast.

00:47:53.480 --> 00:47:58.430
She runs faster than dragon, dumpedy and me.

00:47:58.480 --> 00:48:01.430
Okay, say dumpedy and I.

00:48:01.480 --> 00:48:04.430
We look at dragon.

00:48:04.480 --> 00:48:07.430
She's shaking again.

00:48:07.480 --> 00:48:11.430
Why are you laughing at us again, we ask.

00:48:11.480 --> 00:48:16.430
I'm not laughing at you, says a strange voice.

00:48:16.480 --> 00:48:18.430
It isn't dragon's voice.

00:48:18.480 --> 00:48:24.430
Her voice is high and loud and this voice is low and quiet.

00:48:24.480 --> 00:48:26.430
We're afraid.

00:48:26.480 --> 00:48:29.430
Who is speaking, we ask.

00:48:29.480 --> 00:48:34.430
It's me, answers the strange voice.

00:48:34.480 --> 00:48:40.430
We look around but we only can see mum, dad and dragon.

00:48:40.480 --> 00:48:43.430
Suddenly, smiley cries.

00:48:43.480 --> 00:48:45.430
It's dragon's voice.

00:48:45.480 --> 00:48:49.430
She's got a new voice.

00:48:49.480 --> 00:48:52.430
It's magic, says dumpedy.

00:48:52.480 --> 00:48:54.430
We look at dragon.

00:48:54.480 --> 00:48:56.430
She looks strange.

00:48:56.480 --> 00:49:01.430
She's shaking and her eyes are very bright.

00:49:01.480 --> 00:49:03.430
Mum, cries smiley.

00:49:03.480 --> 00:49:07.430
What's the matter with dragon?

00:49:07.480 --> 00:49:09.430
Mum comes up to dragon.

00:49:09.480 --> 00:49:14.430
She looks at her, touches her head and says dragon.

00:49:14.480 --> 00:49:16.430
You are ill.

00:49:16.480 --> 00:49:18.430
You have got a cold.

00:49:18.480 --> 00:49:20.430
You've got a high temperature.

00:49:20.480 --> 00:49:29.430
I have got a headache and a sore throat, says poor dragon and sneezes.

00:49:29.480 --> 00:49:34.430
And your nose is running, says dad.

00:49:34.480 --> 00:49:37.430
It's the rain.

00:49:37.480 --> 00:49:41.430
Rain's are very cold in Africa.

00:49:41.480 --> 00:49:44.430
You must never dance in the rain again.

00:49:44.480 --> 00:49:47.430
It's dangerous.

00:49:47.480 --> 00:49:50.430
We are sorry for dragon.

00:49:50.480 --> 00:49:56.430
She is sometimes very bad but now she is so sad.

00:49:56.480 --> 00:50:00.430
Don't be sad, dragon, says dumpedy.

00:50:00.480 --> 00:50:02.430
We like your new voice.

00:50:02.480 --> 00:50:06.430
It's so quiet.

00:50:06.480 --> 00:50:09.430
But dragon isn't happy.

00:50:09.480 --> 00:50:12.430
She starts crying.

00:50:12.480 --> 00:50:17.430
We can bring you some sweet seeds, says dumpedy.

00:50:17.480 --> 00:50:20.430
I think it's very boring to be ill.

00:50:20.480 --> 00:50:25.430
So we can stay with you all day, smile smiley.

00:50:25.480 --> 00:50:28.430
And tell you funny stories.

00:50:28.480 --> 00:50:32.430
And bring you water from the river, I say.

00:50:32.480 --> 00:50:36.480
And brush your feathers for you, smile smiley.

00:50:37.480 --> 00:50:39.430
What's the matter?

00:50:39.480 --> 00:50:42.430
Dragon looks very strange again.

00:50:42.480 --> 00:50:45.430
I can't understand why.

00:50:45.480 --> 00:50:47.430
I look and look.

00:50:47.480 --> 00:50:51.430
And suddenly I understand.

00:50:51.480 --> 00:50:54.430
Dragon is smiling.

00:50:54.480 --> 00:50:57.430
She's got a new face now.

00:50:57.480 --> 00:51:00.430
A kind, cute face.

00:51:00.480 --> 00:51:05.430
Oh, it's magic.

00:51:05.480 --> 00:51:14.430
Chapter 14.

00:51:14.480 --> 00:51:19.430
A new name.

00:51:19.480 --> 00:51:23.430
So we stay with dragon all day.

00:51:23.480 --> 00:51:28.430
Sometimes dumpedy goes and brings sweet seeds.

00:51:28.480 --> 00:51:33.430
Or I go to the river and bring some water in my beak for dragon.

00:51:33.480 --> 00:51:40.430
Smiley tells stories to her and brushes dragon's feathers.

00:51:40.480 --> 00:51:44.430
Mum stays with dragon too.

00:51:44.480 --> 00:51:52.430
She keeps her warm when dragon starts shaking and covers her from the sun.

00:51:52.480 --> 00:51:55.430
Dragon is better now.

00:51:55.480 --> 00:52:02.430
She listens to smiley, eats the seeds and drinks the water.

00:52:02.480 --> 00:52:06.430
She isn't shaking anymore.

00:52:06.480 --> 00:52:10.430
Suddenly I can hear a voice.

00:52:10.480 --> 00:52:12.430
I know this voice.

00:52:12.480 --> 00:52:14.430
I like it.

00:52:14.480 --> 00:52:18.430
It is my favorite voice.

00:52:18.480 --> 00:52:20.430
Hello.

00:52:20.480 --> 00:52:23.430
Why are you not playing today?

00:52:23.480 --> 00:52:25.430
Asks the voice.

00:52:25.480 --> 00:52:29.430
I turn round and see softy.

00:52:29.480 --> 00:52:32.430
I am very happy.

00:52:32.480 --> 00:52:36.430
And I say, because dragon is ill.

00:52:36.480 --> 00:52:40.430
Suddenly softy is very sad.

00:52:40.480 --> 00:52:43.430
I know, she says.

00:52:43.480 --> 00:52:45.430
You don't want to play with me.

00:52:45.480 --> 00:52:47.430
You don't like me.

00:52:47.480 --> 00:52:49.430
I'm going away.

00:52:49.480 --> 00:52:53.430
She turns and starts walking away.

00:52:53.480 --> 00:52:55.430
Softy, please.

00:52:55.480 --> 00:52:57.430
Don't go away, I cry.

00:52:57.480 --> 00:52:58.430
I like you.

00:52:58.480 --> 00:53:00.430
You're so nice.

00:53:00.480 --> 00:53:04.430
Why do you always run away?

00:53:04.480 --> 00:53:09.430
But, say softy, what about dragons?

00:53:09.480 --> 00:53:17.430
Why do you always talk about dragons when I want to play with you?

00:53:17.480 --> 00:53:23.430
Because dragon is our sister, I say.

00:53:23.480 --> 00:53:26.430
What?

00:53:26.480 --> 00:53:31.430
Softy's eyes become bigger than her head.

00:53:31.480 --> 00:53:32.430
Look.

00:53:32.480 --> 00:53:35.430
Here she is, I say.

00:53:35.480 --> 00:53:37.430
She's ill today.

00:53:37.480 --> 00:53:43.430
We're staying with her because it's very boring to be ill.

00:53:43.480 --> 00:53:46.430
Softy looks at dragon.

00:53:46.480 --> 00:53:51.430
Dragon isn't that old dragon anymore.

00:53:51.480 --> 00:53:53.430
She's new dragon now.

00:53:53.480 --> 00:53:57.430
She's got a kind smile.

00:53:57.480 --> 00:53:59.430
Are you dragon?

00:53:59.480 --> 00:54:02.430
Ask softy.

00:54:02.480 --> 00:54:06.430
Yes, I am, answers dragon.

00:54:06.480 --> 00:54:10.430
But dragons are ugly, angry monsters.

00:54:10.480 --> 00:54:12.430
Say softy.

00:54:12.480 --> 00:54:13.430
What?

00:54:13.480 --> 00:54:16.430
Crys dragon.

00:54:16.480 --> 00:54:20.430
We can't see her smile anymore.

00:54:20.480 --> 00:54:23.430
She's our old dragon now.

00:54:23.480 --> 00:54:28.430
I'm not an ugly, angry monster.

00:54:28.480 --> 00:54:32.430
And you are dragon, says Mum.

00:54:32.480 --> 00:54:35.430
That ostrich girl is right.

00:54:35.480 --> 00:54:40.430
Dragon means a terrible ugly monster.

00:54:40.480 --> 00:54:43.430
It likes eating other animals.

00:54:43.480 --> 00:54:47.430
It can even eat an ostrich.

00:54:47.480 --> 00:54:51.430
I think you should change your name.

00:54:51.480 --> 00:54:59.430
Oh, now I understand why you always run away, I say, to softy.

00:54:59.480 --> 00:55:02.430
Then it's true.

00:55:02.480 --> 00:55:07.430
You like me and want to play with me, smile softy.

00:55:07.480 --> 00:55:11.430
Of course, I smile at her.

00:55:11.480 --> 00:55:14.430
Dragon is very quiet now.

00:55:14.480 --> 00:55:16.430
She looks at us.

00:55:16.480 --> 00:55:18.430
She looks at Mum.

00:55:18.480 --> 00:55:25.430
And then she says, I don't want to be dragon anymore.

00:55:25.480 --> 00:55:28.430
Help me to find a nice name.

00:55:28.480 --> 00:55:32.430
We can't believe our ears.

00:55:32.480 --> 00:55:38.430
Dragon is really asking us to help her.

00:55:38.480 --> 00:55:42.430
Do you like the sun, asks Mum?

00:55:42.480 --> 00:55:44.430
Yes, I like it.

00:55:44.480 --> 00:55:51.430
It is very hot and dries us when we are wet, says dragon and coughs.

00:55:51.480 --> 00:55:54.430
Do you want to be sunny?

00:55:54.480 --> 00:55:56.430
Asks Mum.

00:55:56.480 --> 00:55:59.430
Oh, that's great, cries dragon.

00:55:59.480 --> 00:56:02.430
I like this name.

00:56:02.480 --> 00:56:05.430
Our dragon likes something.

00:56:05.480 --> 00:56:07.430
It is magic.

00:56:07.480 --> 00:56:09.430
Oh, I'm wrong.

00:56:09.480 --> 00:56:11.430
Our sister isn't dragon anymore.

00:56:11.480 --> 00:56:15.480
Now she is sunny.

00:56:23.480 --> 00:56:26.430
Chapter 15.

00:56:26.480 --> 00:56:29.480
A big day.

00:56:30.480 --> 00:56:32.430
Look at us.

00:56:32.480 --> 00:56:34.430
We're bigger now.

00:56:34.480 --> 00:56:37.430
Our legs are stronger.

00:56:37.480 --> 00:56:40.430
Dumpty is taller than Dad.

00:56:40.480 --> 00:56:44.430
And smiley is fatter than Mum.

00:56:44.480 --> 00:56:48.430
We are almost grown-ups.

00:56:48.480 --> 00:56:51.430
We don't walk with Mum and Dad anymore.

00:56:51.480 --> 00:56:56.430
We walk with other young ostriches.

00:56:56.480 --> 00:57:00.430
There are a lot of them in our group.

00:57:00.480 --> 00:57:03.430
Softy is with us too.

00:57:03.480 --> 00:57:05.430
No.

00:57:05.480 --> 00:57:08.430
She is with me.

00:57:08.480 --> 00:57:11.430
We want to be together all our life.

00:57:11.480 --> 00:57:14.430
We want to have a family.

00:57:14.480 --> 00:57:18.430
We want to have sons and daughters.

00:57:18.480 --> 00:57:23.430
I want to call my son and daughter Dumpty and smiley

00:57:23.480 --> 00:57:27.430
because I love my brother and sister.

00:57:27.480 --> 00:57:31.430
Softy has got a brother and sister too.

00:57:31.480 --> 00:57:35.430
Their names are foodie and tallie.

00:57:35.480 --> 00:57:38.430
It is because her brother likes eating.

00:57:38.480 --> 00:57:42.430
And her sister is the tallest in the family.

00:57:42.480 --> 00:57:46.480
She is even taller than her father.

00:57:51.480 --> 00:57:54.430
Two months pass.

00:57:54.480 --> 00:57:59.430
Softy and I have got a nest now.

00:57:59.480 --> 00:58:02.430
It is on the ground.

00:58:02.480 --> 00:58:05.430
There are three eggs in the nest.

00:58:05.480 --> 00:58:08.430
I guard our chicks at night.

00:58:08.480 --> 00:58:12.430
And softy does it by day.

00:58:12.480 --> 00:58:15.430
The great day comes.

00:58:15.480 --> 00:58:19.430
The first egg breaks into small pieces.

00:58:19.480 --> 00:58:22.430
And we can see our son.

00:58:22.480 --> 00:58:27.430
He has got very big feet.

00:58:27.480 --> 00:58:30.430
Our son is very clever.

00:58:30.480 --> 00:58:33.430
Laughs softy.

00:58:33.480 --> 00:58:36.430
Why? I ask.

00:58:36.480 --> 00:58:38.430
He knows our problem.

00:58:38.480 --> 00:58:39.430
Look.

00:58:39.480 --> 00:58:42.430
He has got very big feet.

00:58:42.480 --> 00:58:46.430
So his name must be footy.

00:58:46.480 --> 00:58:50.430
It is half foodie and half Dumpty.

00:58:50.480 --> 00:58:54.430
Our good boy. I smile.

00:58:54.480 --> 00:59:00.430
Here comes our daughter, say softy, when the second egg breaks.

00:59:00.480 --> 00:59:04.430
Why is she so small, I ask?

00:59:04.480 --> 00:59:07.430
I am worried.

00:59:07.480 --> 00:59:10.430
Don't worry, say softy.

00:59:10.480 --> 00:59:12.430
She must be small.

00:59:12.480 --> 00:59:15.430
Why? I ask again.

00:59:15.480 --> 00:59:18.430
Think dear, say softy.

00:59:18.480 --> 00:59:20.430
I think and think.

00:59:20.480 --> 00:59:24.430
And then I understand.

00:59:24.480 --> 00:59:28.430
It's because her name must be smally.

00:59:28.480 --> 00:59:32.430
It's half smiley and half tally.

00:59:32.480 --> 00:59:35.430
Yes, say softy.

00:59:35.480 --> 00:59:40.430
Our children are very young, but very clever.

00:59:40.480 --> 00:59:42.430
We look at the third egg.

00:59:42.480 --> 00:59:45.430
It is breaking now too.

00:59:45.480 --> 00:59:49.430
Our second daughter is coming out.

00:59:49.480 --> 00:59:52.430
She is cute.

00:59:52.480 --> 00:59:58.430
She has got yellow feathers and a long slim neck.

00:59:58.480 --> 01:00:03.430
Let's call her slimmy, say softy.

01:00:03.480 --> 01:00:06.430
No, say our daughter.

01:00:06.480 --> 01:00:09.430
I don't like this name.

01:00:09.480 --> 01:00:13.430
What about yellow? I ask.

01:00:13.480 --> 01:00:18.430
No, she says again.

01:00:18.480 --> 01:00:21.430
Oh, no, I cry.

01:00:21.480 --> 01:00:23.430
It's dragon.

01:00:23.480 --> 01:00:28.430
Our daughter looks at the sky and sees the sun.

01:00:28.480 --> 01:00:31.430
What is this? She asks.

01:00:31.480 --> 01:00:35.430
It's the sun answers softy.

01:00:35.480 --> 01:00:38.430
I am very quiet now.

01:00:38.480 --> 01:00:41.430
I am looking at my daughter.

01:00:41.480 --> 01:00:45.430
I can see her nice face.

01:00:45.480 --> 01:00:48.430
Of course she isn't dragon.

01:00:48.480 --> 01:00:55.480
My name is Sunny, she says, and smiles.
